WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Off-Ball Lens: see receiving opportunities before the touch.
College of Engineering Football. Actual local v3 demonstration.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Follow A7: check back, curve inside, then accelerate.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
The field shows direct receiving space.
Ball flight hides unsupported values.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:28.800
AS and DAS come from the published accessible-space model.
Area and danger-weighted area, not probability or causal credit.

5
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:37.300
An option can remain unused.
The carrier chooses a different teammate.

6
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:46.800
Timing matters: A7 is screened out during the point-based offside interval.

7
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000
A real Microsoft Agent Framework Agent requests evidence from the play so far.

8
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:02.200
Azure gpt-5-mini selects claims; the application validates every displayed fact.

9
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:10.200
One Agent, two native tools: analyze_window and get_evidence.

10
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:15.000
Click an evidence frame to revisit the opportunity.
Old answers clear on a new context.

11
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.000
English and Chinese; a simpler Fan view and a detailed Analyst view.

12
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:27.300
Synthetic data, reproducible evidence, explicit limits.
Direct receiving space does not capture the full value of every run.

13
00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:53.400
Off-Ball Lens: the run before the touch.
Source and replay: github.com/cabbage1999/Off-Ball-Lens.
The Azure Agent is shown on the local build.
